                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2644e887-f811-3b66-98c2-bb4112a36f9e",
                        "entry_id": "3301bcf1-c97d-34da-985e-a5700ebbee3b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "архит. связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным фахверк; свойственный, характерный для фахверка"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e922a0f-c965-4e57-9f5f-72a5e8b40735",
                                "sense_id": "2644e887-f811-3b66-98c2-bb4112a36f9e",
                                "text": "За пять лет, что я не видел Софии, в ней успели построить очень хорошие, совсем европейские дома; но большинство домов, особенно на окраинах, были старые, фахверковой постройки, зимой холодные."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "792ff9a3-b8e4-45e3-9983-5ebe4ce3b932",
                        "source_entry_id": "3301bcf1-c97d-34da-985e-a5700ebbee3b",
                        "source_sense_id": "2644e887-f811-3b66-98c2-bb4112a36f9e",
                        "target_lang_word": "framework",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "framework",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22ac2cd0-8a74-360d-a5d8-e7a45cb23603",
                                        "entry_id": "fe5e1e72-70dd-3cf7-8b20-7b9c30445515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A support structure comprising joined parts or conglomerated particles and intervening open spaces of similar or larger size."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28fcdc33-cf54-341d-b855-3a1dcf156f1e",
                                        "entry_id": "fe5e1e72-70dd-3cf7-8b20-7b9c30445515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The arrangement of support beams that represent a building's general shape and size."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b730bd83-1c1c-3675-9328-da99d40d31b4",
                                        "entry_id": "fe5e1e72-70dd-3cf7-8b20-7b9c30445515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The larger branches of a tree that determine its shape."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e11284a1-4ed8-3d92-a50f-0adbb14a3efa",
                                        "entry_id": "fe5e1e72-70dd-3cf7-8b20-7b9c30445515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A basic conceptual structure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba52a3e9-05ae-4092-9207-f77b7513ace5",
                                                "sense_id": "e11284a1-4ed8-3d92-a50f-0adbb14a3efa",
                                                "text": "These ‘three principles of connexion’ compose the framework of principles in Hume's account of the association of ideas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b309e1e7-283f-4cb2-ac77-81646b2798ef",
                                                "sense_id": "e11284a1-4ed8-3d92-a50f-0adbb14a3efa",
                                                "text": "He draws eclectically on studies of baboons, descriptive anthropological accounts of hunter-gatherer societies and, in a few cases, the fossil record. With this biological framework in place, Corning endeavors to show that the capitalist system as currently practiced in the United States and elsewhere is manifestly unfair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67af408c-2a4d-3b9f-8965-18f4ceeea65c",
                                        "entry_id": "fe5e1e72-70dd-3cf7-8b20-7b9c30445515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A reusable piece of code (and, sometimes, other utilities) providing a standard environment within which an application can be implemented."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5083061b-021c-3a6a-baf1-18350bfb334e",
                                        "entry_id": "fe5e1e72-70dd-3cf7-8b20-7b9c30445515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An established and structured system of rules and principles used for analyzing and describing the structure of a language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "504ad9ca-d86e-491d-9df4-58c7bac6fc37",
                        "source_entry_id": "3301bcf1-c97d-34da-985e-a5700ebbee3b",
                        "source_sense_id": "2644e887-f811-3b66-98c2-bb4112a36f9e",
                        "target_lang_word": "frame-built",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c5e92ea-7626-4364-b5d7-c85de5d69530",
                        "source_entry_id": "3301bcf1-c97d-34da-985e-a5700ebbee3b",
                        "source_sense_id": "2644e887-f811-3b66-98c2-bb4112a36f9e",
                        "target_lang_word": "half-timbered",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "half-timbered",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                        "entry_id": "61f54f0c-b0ad-3b7e-a8c9-42d8cf20de27",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a building: constructed using a load-bearing timber frame with the spaces (panels) between the timbers filled with bricks, stone, or wattle and daub, etc. (the infill), especially if the timber frame is visible on the outside of the building."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03d458ed-5c21-4b8c-82ac-cd3c1c128b0e",
                                                "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                                "text": "Having ideally supposed that the County Town must be superior to all others in point of beauty and extent, we were disappointed to find it a small place, consisting of about a hundred half-timbered houses forming a miserable street."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b00681b-dfca-400f-b35a-06a156a2b0e5",
                                                "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                                "text": "The construction here described, is exactly similar to that followed in the old half timbered houses of England."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dda68c5-3b15-4a78-b88f-b34fd309457c",
                                                "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                                "text": "Some of the streets are very narrow, with old half timbered houses on each side; Crown-street is a specimen of the early style of its street architecture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78c5018f-dbac-4936-8fff-2a58ebdf06bc",
                                                "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                                "text": "The Tullivers had lived on this spot for generations, and he had sat listening on a low stool on winter evenings while his father talked of the old half-timbered mill that had been there before the last great floods which damaged it so that his grandfather pulled it down and built the new one."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e9c0ee8-0b58-40ff-a12e-71077bd77b0a",
                                                "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                                "text": "The old houses, however, were left until the great fire of 1666 swept them away: it was these charming half-timbered dwellings which afforded the chief fuel for that huge bonfire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7aee2b50-ab96-49b5-b78c-15b4eca81145",
                                                "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                                "text": "Modeled upon a style popular in England in the middle of the seventeenth century, the many-gabled, half-timbered house still stands, testimony to the skill of its builder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fec2efb-fca7-4df2-9cb7-71e299e138d2",
                                                "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                                "text": "This half-timbered building is the birthplace of William Shakespeare. In this house, he and his brothers and sisters were born and raised."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ec96c2f-dd71-43f3-9936-c6de1c68714d",
                                                "sense_id": "fafd4197-1d2b-3594-b008-9f54cde4a350",
                                                "text": "We pass Much and Little Marcle, and Dymock, all ancient sounding and through the waking up heart of the half-timbered market town of Ledbury, dating to the Doomsday Book."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
